STORIES_LOAD("1sm",{"s1a":{"passage":[[1,1,28]],"intro":[{"sc":"tabernacle","n":"Hannah longed for a baby, but year after year, none came. Her husband's other wife, Peninnah, had children, and she teased Hannah cruelly until she cried and couldn't eat."},{"sc":"tabernacle","n":"At God's tent in Shiloh, Hannah prayed with all her heart. Her lips moved, but no sound came out."},{"sc":"tabernacle","w":"beli","e":"frown","t":"How long will you be drunk? Put away your wine!"},{"sc":"tabernacle","w":"bhannah","e":"worried","t":"No, my lord! I'm not drunk. I'm a woman with a broken heart, pouring out my soul to the Lord."},{"sc":"tabernacle","w":"beli","e":"smile","t":"Go in peace. May the God of Israel give you what you have asked."},{"sc":"tabernacle","n":"God answered. Hannah had a son, and named him Samuel, 'heard by God'. When he was old enough, she brought him to Eli to serve God for life, just as she had promised."}],"lesson":{"title":"Pour out your heart","text":"Hannah didn't pretend to be fine. She took her pain to God honestly, even when others misunderstood her. Then she kept her promise, even though it cost her. Leaders pray honestly and keep their word."},"order":["Hannah longs for a baby","Peninnah teases her","Hannah prays silently at Shiloh","Eli thinks she is drunk","Samuel is born","Hannah brings Samuel to serve God"],"quiz":[{"q":"Why did Eli think Hannah was drunk?","o":["Her lips moved but no sound came out","She was singing loudly","She fell over","She was laughing"],"why":"1 Samuel 1:13."},{"q":"What does the name Samuel mean?","o":["Heard by God","Gift","Strong","Prince"],"why":"God heard her prayer."},{"q":"What did Hannah do when Samuel was old enough?","o":["Brought him to serve God, as she promised","Kept him at home","Sent him to Egypt","Made him king"],"why":"1 Samuel 1:28."}],"words":["HANNAH","PRAYER","SHILOH","ELI","SAMUEL","PROMISE"]},"s1b":{"passage":[[2,1,10],[2,12,26]],"intro":[{"sc":"tabernacle","w":"bhannah","e":"big","t":"My heart is glad in the Lord! There is no one holy like the Lord. There is no Rock like our God! He lifts the poor from the dust and seats them with princes!"},{"sc":"altar","n":"But Eli's two sons, Hophni and Phinehas, were priests who didn't care about God at all. They grabbed the best meat from people's offerings by force before it was given to God."},{"sc":"altar","n":"They did other wicked things too. Eli heard about it and scolded them, but he never stopped them."},{"sc":"tabernacle","n":"Meanwhile, little Samuel served God faithfully, wearing a small linen robe. Every year Hannah made him a new little coat. And Samuel grew in favour with God and with people."}],"lesson":{"title":"Same place, different hearts","text":"Samuel and Eli's sons grew up in the very same place, around the very same holy things. The sons became greedy and careless; Samuel grew close to God. Being near holy things doesn't make you holy. Your choices do."},"order":["Hannah sings a song of praise","Eli's sons take meat by force","Eli scolds them but doesn't stop them","Samuel serves God in a linen robe","Hannah brings Samuel a new coat every year"],"quiz":[{"q":"Who were Eli's wicked sons?","o":["Hophni and Phinehas","Cain and Abel","Jacob and Esau","Saul and Jonathan"],"why":"1 Samuel 2:34."},{"q":"What did Hannah bring Samuel every year?","o":["A new little coat","Food","Toys","Money"],"why":"1 Samuel 2:19."},{"q":"What did Hannah call God in her song?","o":["The Rock","The Tower","The River","The Star"],"why":"1 Samuel 2:2."}],"words":["SONG","ROCK","HOPHNI","GREEDY","COAT","FAVOUR"]},"s1c":{"passage":[[3,1,21]],"intro":[{"sc":"lamp","n":"In those days, God rarely spoke to anyone. One night, old Eli was asleep in his room, and the boy Samuel was lying down near the ark of God. The lamp of God was still burning."},{"sc":"lamp","n":"\"Samuel!\" Samuel jumped up and ran to Eli. \"Here I am!\" \"I didn't call you. Go back to bed.\" It happened again. And again."},{"sc":"lamp","w":"beli","e":"smile","t":"It must be the Lord calling you. If He calls again, say: 'Speak, Lord, for your servant is listening.'"},{"sc":"lamp","w":"bsamboy","e":"big","t":"Speak, Lord, for your servant is listening!"},{"sc":"lamp","n":"God told Samuel that Eli's family would be judged for his sons' wickedness. In the morning, Samuel was afraid to tell Eli, but Eli insisted, and Samuel told him everything."},{"sc":"tabernacle","n":"As Samuel grew up, God was with him, and everyone in Israel knew that Samuel was a true prophet."}],"lesson":{"title":"Learn to listen","text":"Samuel didn't recognise God's voice at first. He needed an older person to help him. And when God spoke, Samuel told the truth, even when it was hard. Leaders listen to God, and they're brave enough to share hard truths kindly."},"order":["Samuel sleeps near the ark","He hears his name called","He runs to Eli three times","Eli tells him to answer God","Samuel says, \"Speak, Lord\"","Samuel tells Eli the hard message"],"quiz":[{"q":"Who did Samuel think was calling him?","o":["Eli","His mother","An angel","A friend"],"why":"He ran to Eli three times."},{"q":"What did Eli tell Samuel to say?","o":["\"Speak, Lord, for your servant is listening\"","\"Go away\"","\"Who are you?\"","\"I'm sleeping\""],"why":"1 Samuel 3:9."},{"q":"Was Samuel brave enough to tell Eli the message?","o":["Yes, he told him everything","No, he hid","He lied","He ran away"],"why":"1 Samuel 3:18."}],"words":["SAMUEL","LISTEN","SPEAK","LAMP","NIGHT","CALL"]},"s1d":{"passage":[[4,1,22]],"intro":[{"sc":"battlehill","n":"Israel lost a battle against the Philistines. The leaders had an idea: \"Let's bring the ark of God into battle. It'll be like a good luck charm!\""},{"sc":"battlehill","n":"When the ark arrived, Israel's army shouted so loud the ground shook. The Philistines were terrified, but they fought even harder."},{"sc":"battlehill","n":"Israel was crushed. Eli's wicked sons, Hophni and Phinehas, were killed, and the ark of God was captured!"},{"sc":"tabernacle","n":"Old Eli, 98 years old and nearly blind, was sitting by the road waiting for news. When he heard the ark was taken, he fell backwards off his seat and died."},{"sc":"tabernacle","n":"That same day, Phinehas's wife gave birth to a son. She named him Ichabod, which means 'the glory is gone', because the ark of God had been taken."}],"lesson":{"title":"God is not a lucky charm","text":"Israel treated the ark like magic, not like the presence of a holy God. They wanted God's power without God's ways. Leaders don't use God as a tool to get what they want; they follow Him."},"order":["Israel loses a battle","They bring the ark like a lucky charm","Israel loses again, and the ark is captured","Eli's sons are killed","Eli falls and dies","A baby is named Ichabod"],"quiz":[{"q":"Why did Israel bring the ark into battle?","o":["They used it like a lucky charm","God told them to","To show it off","To hide it"],"why":"1 Samuel 4:3."},{"q":"What happened to the ark?","o":["The Philistines captured it","It was burned","It flew away","It was buried"],"why":"1 Samuel 4:11."},{"q":"What does Ichabod mean?","o":["The glory is gone","Strong","Laughter","Gift of God"],"why":"1 Samuel 4:21."}],"words":["ARK","CAPTURED","ICHABOD","GLORY","ELI","PHILISTINES"]},"s1e":{"passage":[[5,1,12],[6,7,16]],"intro":[{"sc":"dagon","n":"The proud Philistines carried the ark into the temple of their god, Dagon, and set it next to his big statue. A trophy!"},{"sc":"dagon","n":"Next morning: Dagon had fallen flat on his face in front of the ark of the Lord! They stood him back up."},{"sc":"dagon","n":"The morning after: Dagon had fallen on his face again, and this time his head and hands were broken off on the doorstep!"},{"sc":"dagon","n":"Then the people of the town broke out in painful lumps, and rats spread everywhere. They moved the ark to another town, and the same thing happened. And another!"},{"sc":"battlehill","n":"Finally they put the ark on a new cart pulled by two mother cows, and let the cows go wherever they wanted. The cows walked straight back to Israel, mooing all the way!"}],"lesson":{"title":"Nothing can stand before God","text":"The Philistines thought they had beaten Israel's God. But their idol fell on its face, twice. God doesn't need people to defend His honour. Leaders put their trust in the real God, not in things that can fall over."},"order":["The ark is put in Dagon's temple","Dagon falls on his face","They stand him back up","Dagon falls again and breaks","The people get painful lumps","Cows carry the ark back to Israel"],"quiz":[{"q":"What happened to Dagon's statue?","o":["It fell on its face, twice","It started talking","It grew bigger","Nothing"],"why":"1 Samuel 5:3-4."},{"q":"What broke off the second time?","o":["Its head and hands","Its feet","Its crown","Its base"],"why":"1 Samuel 5:4."},{"q":"What carried the ark back to Israel?","o":["Two mother cows pulling a cart","Soldiers","Camels","A boat"],"why":"1 Samuel 6:12."}],"words":["DAGON","STATUE","FELL","CART","COWS","IDOL"]},"s1f":{"passage":[[7,3,17]],"intro":[{"sc":"stone","w":"bsamuel","e":"stern","t":"If you really want to return to the Lord, throw away your idols and serve Him only. Then He will rescue you."},{"sc":"stone","n":"The people obeyed. They gathered at Mizpah, poured out water before the Lord, fasted and confessed their sins."},{"sc":"battlehill","n":"The Philistines heard and attacked. The people were terrified. Samuel prayed. And God thundered with a mighty voice from heaven! The Philistines panicked and ran."},{"sc":"stone","n":"Samuel set up a large stone and called it Ebenezer, which means 'stone of help'. \"Up to now, the Lord has helped us!\""}],"lesson":{"title":"Mark the moments God helps you","text":"Samuel built a reminder stone so they'd never forget what God did. When you look back on how God has helped you before, it gives you courage for what's ahead. Leaders help people remember."},"order":["Samuel tells the people to throw away idols","They gather at Mizpah and confess","The Philistines attack","Samuel prays","God thunders and the enemy runs","Samuel sets up the Ebenezer stone"],"quiz":[{"q":"What does Ebenezer mean?","o":["Stone of help","Big rock","Victory","Home"],"why":"1 Samuel 7:12."},{"q":"What did God send against the Philistines?","o":["Loud thunder","Frogs","Hail","A flood"],"why":"1 Samuel 7:10."},{"q":"What did the people throw away first?","o":["Their idols","Their swords","Their food","Their tents"],"why":"1 Samuel 7:4."}],"words":["EBENEZER","STONE","HELP","THUNDER","MIZPAH","IDOLS"]},"s1g":{"passage":[[8,1,22]],"intro":[{"sc":"citygate","n":"Samuel grew old. His sons were supposed to lead after him, but they took bribes and were unfair."},{"sc":"citygate","w":"bpeople","e":"stern","t":"You're old, and your sons don't follow your ways. Give us a king, like all the other nations have!"},{"sc":"citygate","n":"Samuel was upset. But God said: \"They haven't rejected you. They've rejected Me as their King.\""},{"sc":"citygate","w":"bsamuel","e":"stern","t":"A king will take your sons for his army, your daughters for his kitchens, your best fields and a tenth of your harvest. One day you'll cry out because of him!"},{"sc":"citygate","w":"bpeople","e":"frown","t":"No! We want a king! We want to be like everyone else!"}],"lesson":{"title":"Don't just copy everyone else","text":"Israel wanted a king mainly so they could be 'like all the other nations'. Wanting to fit in can make us reject what's best for us. Leaders ask what's right, not just what everyone else is doing."},"order":["Samuel grows old","His sons take bribes","The people ask for a king","God says they have rejected Him","Samuel warns them what a king will take","The people still insist on a king"],"quiz":[{"q":"Why did the people want a king?","o":["To be like all the other nations","Samuel asked them to","They had lots of gold","God told them to"],"why":"1 Samuel 8:5."},{"q":"Who did God say they were really rejecting?","o":["God Himself","Samuel","Moses","Nobody"],"why":"1 Samuel 8:7."},{"q":"What did Samuel warn a king would do?","o":["Take their sons, daughters, fields and harvest","Make them all rich","Build them houses","Nothing"],"why":"1 Samuel 8:11-17."}],"words":["KING","NATIONS","BRIBES","WARNING","REJECT","SAMUEL"]},"s1h":{"passage":[[9,1,10],[9,15,21],[10,1,1],[10,17,24]],"intro":[{"sc":"donkeys","n":"A young man named Saul was sent to look for his father's lost donkeys. He was handsome, and a head taller than everyone else!"},{"sc":"donkeys","n":"After days of searching, his servant said, \"There's a man of God in this town. Maybe he can tell us where the donkeys are!\""},{"sc":"tents","n":"That man was Samuel. God had told him the day before: \"Tomorrow I'll send you the man who will be king.\" Samuel told Saul the donkeys were found, then poured oil on his head."},{"sc":"tents","w":"bsaul","e":"worried","t":"Me? I'm from the smallest tribe, and my family is the least important in it!"},{"sc":"citygate","n":"Later, all Israel gathered to choose a king by lot. The lot fell on Saul... but he couldn't be found! He was hiding among the luggage!"},{"sc":"citygate","n":"They pulled him out. He stood a head taller than everyone. Samuel said, \"Here is the man the Lord has chosen!\" And the people shouted, \"Long live the king!\""}],"lesson":{"title":"Humble beginnings","text":"Saul went looking for donkeys and found a crown. At first he was humble, so humble he hid! Humility is a great start for a leader. The question is whether you stay humble when the crown is on your head."},"order":["Saul looks for lost donkeys","His servant suggests asking the man of God","Samuel pours oil on Saul's head","Israel gathers to choose a king","Saul hides among the luggage","The people shout, \"Long live the king!\""],"quiz":[{"q":"What was Saul looking for?","o":["His father's lost donkeys","A crown","Samuel","A wife"],"why":"1 Samuel 9:3."},{"q":"How tall was Saul?","o":["A head taller than everyone","Very short","Average","A giant"],"why":"1 Samuel 9:2."},{"q":"Where was Saul hiding when he was chosen king?","o":["Among the luggage","In a cave","Up a tree","In a well"],"why":"1 Samuel 10:22."}],"words":["SAUL","DONKEYS","OIL","LUGGAGE","TALL","KING"]},"s1i":{"passage":[[11,1,15]],"intro":[{"sc":"citygate","n":"A cruel king named Nahash surrounded the town of Jabesh-gilead. The people begged for peace."},{"sc":"citygate","n":"Nahash's terms were horrible: \"I'll make peace if I can gouge out everyone's right eye, to bring shame on all Israel!\" The people asked for seven days to find help."},{"sc":"ploughfield","n":"Saul was coming home from ploughing his field when he heard the news. The Spirit of God came on him, and he burned with anger at the injustice."},{"sc":"ploughfield","w":"bsaul","e":"stern","t":"Whoever doesn't follow Saul and Samuel, let it be done to his oxen!"},{"sc":"battlehill","n":"330,000 men joined him! Before sunrise they attacked and rescued the town. Some wanted to punish those who had doubted Saul, but he said, \"No one will be put to death today, for today the Lord has rescued Israel.\""}],"lesson":{"title":"Stand up for the helpless, and be gracious","text":"Saul's first act as king was rescuing people facing cruelty. And when he won, he chose mercy instead of revenge on those who had doubted him. Leaders defend the helpless, and they're gracious in victory."},"order":["Nahash surrounds Jabesh","He demands everyone's right eye","Saul hears the news while ploughing","The Spirit of God comes on Saul","Saul's army rescues the town","Saul shows mercy to his doubters"],"quiz":[{"q":"What cruel thing did Nahash demand?","o":["Everyone's right eye","All their gold","Their children","Their cattle"],"why":"1 Samuel 11:2."},{"q":"What was Saul doing when he heard the news?","o":["Coming home from ploughing","Sleeping","Eating","Fighting"],"why":"1 Samuel 11:5."},{"q":"What did Saul say about those who doubted him?","o":["No one will be put to death today","Punish them all","Send them away","Make them slaves"],"why":"1 Samuel 11:13."}],"words":["JABESH","NAHASH","RESCUE","MERCY","SPIRIT","OXEN"]},"s1i2":{"passage":[[12,1,5],[12,16,25]],"intro":[{"sc":"citygate","w":"bsamuel","e":"stern","t":"Here I am. Have I ever stolen anyone's ox or donkey? Have I cheated anyone, or taken a bribe? Tell me, and I'll pay it back!"},{"sc":"citygate","w":"bpeople","e":"smile","t":"You've never cheated us or taken anything from anyone!"},{"sc":"barley","n":"Then Samuel said, \"You asked for a king, and God has given you one. Now watch. It's wheat harvest, when it never rains. I'll ask God to send thunder and rain.\""},{"sc":"barley","n":"Thunder crashed and rain poured down on the dry harvest fields! The people were terrified and asked Samuel to pray for them."},{"sc":"barley","w":"bsamuel","e":"smile","t":"Don't be afraid. Serve the Lord with all your heart. And as for me, far be it from me to sin against the Lord by ever stopping praying for you!"}],"lesson":{"title":"Lead with a clean record","text":"Samuel could stand in front of the whole nation and ask, 'Have I ever cheated anyone?', and nobody could say yes. And even after they rejected his leadership, he promised to keep praying for them. Leaders keep clean hands, and they keep loving people who disappoint them."},"order":["Samuel asks if he ever cheated anyone","The people say he never did","Samuel calls for thunder at harvest","Thunder and rain come","The people are afraid","Samuel promises to keep praying for them"],"quiz":[{"q":"What did Samuel ask the people?","o":["Whether he had ever cheated anyone","For money","To make him king","To leave"],"why":"1 Samuel 12:3."},{"q":"Why was the thunder so surprising?","o":["It was wheat harvest, when it never rains","It was night","It was winter","It was in Egypt"],"why":"1 Samuel 12:17."},{"q":"What did Samuel promise never to stop doing?","o":["Praying for them","Judging them","Taxing them","Leading them"],"why":"1 Samuel 12:23."}],"words":["SAMUEL","THUNDER","HARVEST","HONEST","PRAYING","FAREWELL"]},"s1j":{"passage":[[13,5,14]],"intro":[{"sc":"battlehill","n":"A huge Philistine army gathered, with 30,000 chariots and soldiers like sand on the seashore. Israel's soldiers hid in caves and bushes, and some ran away."},{"sc":"altar","n":"Samuel had told Saul: \"Wait seven days. I'll come and offer the sacrifice.\" Saul waited... and waited... and on the seventh day, Samuel hadn't arrived."},{"sc":"altar","w":"bsaul","e":"worried","t":"My army is running away! I'll offer the sacrifice myself."},{"sc":"altar","n":"As soon as Saul finished, Samuel arrived."},{"sc":"altar","w":"bsamuel","e":"stern","t":"What have you done? You disobeyed the Lord. Now your kingdom will not last. The Lord has found a man after His own heart."}],"lesson":{"title":"Impatience is costly","text":"Saul panicked under pressure and did what only a priest was supposed to do. He chose the quick fix over obedience. Leaders learn to wait on God, especially when everyone around them is panicking."},"order":["A huge Philistine army gathers","Israel's soldiers hide and run","Samuel told Saul to wait seven days","Saul offers the sacrifice himself","Samuel arrives just after","Samuel says Saul's kingdom won't last"],"quiz":[{"q":"How long did Samuel tell Saul to wait?","o":["Seven days","One day","Forty days","One hour"],"why":"1 Samuel 13:8."},{"q":"What did Saul do when Samuel was late?","o":["Offered the sacrifice himself","Waited patiently","Ran away","Prayed quietly"],"why":"1 Samuel 13:9."},{"q":"God was looking for a man after His own...","o":["Heart","Army","Crown","Gold"],"why":"1 Samuel 13:14."}],"words":["WAIT","PATIENCE","SACRIFICE","PANIC","OBEY","HEART"]},"s1j2":{"passage":[[13,19,22]],"intro":[{"sc":"forge","n":"Here's a strange detail. In Saul's day, there wasn't a single blacksmith anywhere in Israel!"},{"sc":"forge","n":"The Philistines had banned them, saying, \"Otherwise the Hebrews will make swords and spears!\""},{"sc":"forge","n":"So whenever an Israelite farmer needed to sharpen his plough, axe or sickle, he had to go down to the Philistines and pay them a high price."},{"sc":"battlehill","n":"On the day of battle, not one soldier in Saul's army had a sword or a spear. Only Saul and his son Jonathan had them. That's the army Jonathan took into his cliff-top adventure!"}],"lesson":{"title":"God isn't limited by what you lack","text":"The enemy controlled the weapons, and Israel's army had almost none. Yet God gave victory, through Jonathan's faith, not through better equipment. Don't wait for perfect resources. Trust God with what you have."},"order":["The Philistines ban blacksmiths in Israel","Farmers must pay Philistines to sharpen tools","Israel's army has no swords","Only Saul and Jonathan have weapons","God still gives victory"],"quiz":[{"q":"Why were there no blacksmiths in Israel?","o":["The Philistines banned them","They all moved away","There was no iron","Saul forbade them"],"why":"1 Samuel 13:19."},{"q":"Who had a sword on the day of battle?","o":["Only Saul and Jonathan","Every soldier","Nobody","Only David"],"why":"1 Samuel 13:22."},{"q":"Where did farmers go to sharpen their tools?","o":["To the Philistines","To Egypt","To the temple","To Samuel"],"why":"1 Samuel 13:20."}],"words":["SWORD","SPEAR","SMITH","PLOUGH","SHARPEN","IRON"]},"s1k":{"passage":[[14,1,15],[14,24,30],[14,43,45]],"intro":[{"sc":"cliffs","n":"Saul's son Jonathan had an idea. He whispered to his young armour-bearer: \"Let's go over to the Philistine camp, just the two of us.\""},{"sc":"cliffs","w":"bjonathan","e":"smile","t":"Nothing can stop the Lord from saving, by many or by few!"},{"sc":"cliffs","n":"They climbed up a steep rocky cliff on their hands and feet. Jonathan fought the guards at the top, and the whole Philistine camp panicked. Then the ground shook!"},{"sc":"battlehill","n":"Israel won a great victory. But Saul had made a foolish order: \"Nobody eat anything until evening!\" Jonathan hadn't heard it, and tasted some honey with the tip of his stick. His eyes brightened."},{"sc":"battlehill","n":"Saul was going to put his own son to death for it! But the people stood up for Jonathan: \"He brought this great victory! Not one hair of his head will fall!\""}],"lesson":{"title":"Bold faith, and wise orders","text":"Jonathan believed God could win with just two people. Saul, meanwhile, made a rash rule that weakened his own tired army and nearly cost his son's life. Leaders take bold steps of faith, and they don't make foolish rules just to look in control."},"order":["Jonathan and his armour-bearer sneak out","They climb a steep cliff","The Philistine camp panics","Saul forbids anyone to eat","Jonathan tastes honey","The people save Jonathan's life"],"quiz":[{"q":"How many went with Jonathan to the Philistine camp?","o":["Just his armour-bearer","An army","Ten men","Saul"],"why":"1 Samuel 14:1."},{"q":"What did Jonathan taste?","o":["Honey","Bread","Wine","Figs"],"why":"1 Samuel 14:27."},{"q":"Who saved Jonathan from his father's order?","o":["The people","Samuel","David","Nobody"],"why":"1 Samuel 14:45."}],"words":["JONATHAN","CLIFF","HONEY","BOLD","ARMOUR","FEW"]},"s1l":{"passage":[[15,1,3],[15,10,28]],"intro":[{"sc":"battlehill","n":"God gave Saul a clear command about the Amalekites, the nation that had attacked Israel from behind when they left Egypt: destroy everything, keep nothing."},{"sc":"battlehill","n":"Saul won the battle. But he kept King Agag alive, and he kept the best sheep and cattle for himself. Then he built a monument to honour... himself."},{"sc":"battlehill","w":"bsaul","e":"smile","t":"I have obeyed the Lord!"},{"sc":"battlehill","w":"bsamuel","e":"stern","t":"Then what is this bleating of sheep in my ears?"},{"sc":"battlehill","w":"bsaul","e":"worried","t":"Oh, the people kept the best animals... to sacrifice to God!"},{"sc":"battlehill","w":"bsamuel","e":"stern","t":"To obey is better than sacrifice. Because you have rejected the Lord's word, He has rejected you as king."},{"sc":"battlehill","n":"As Samuel turned to leave, Saul grabbed his robe, and it tore. \"The Lord has torn the kingdom from you today,\" said Samuel."},{"sc":"battlehill","n":"Then Samuel called for King Agag, whom Saul had spared. Agag came cheerfully, thinking, \"Surely the bitterness of death is past.\" But Samuel carried out God's judgement on the cruel king himself. Samuel never went to see Saul again, but he grieved for him."}],"lesson":{"title":"Half-obedience is disobedience","text":"Saul obeyed partly, then made excuses and blamed the people. He even made a monument to himself. God wants obedience more than impressive offerings. Leaders take responsibility instead of making excuses."},"order":["God gives Saul a clear command","Saul keeps King Agag alive","He keeps the best animals","He builds a monument to himself","Samuel hears sheep bleating","Samuel says, \"To obey is better than sacrifice\""],"quiz":[{"q":"What gave Saul away?","o":["The bleating of sheep","A letter","A spy","His crown"],"why":"1 Samuel 15:14."},{"q":"Who did Saul blame?","o":["The people","Samuel","God","Jonathan"],"why":"1 Samuel 15:15."},{"q":"What tore when Saul grabbed it?","o":["Samuel's robe","A flag","A tent","A scroll"],"why":"1 Samuel 15:27."}],"words":["OBEY","SACRIFICE","AGAG","SHEEP","EXCUSES","ROBE"]},"s1m":{"passage":[[16,1,13]],"intro":[{"sc":"tents","n":"God sent Samuel to Bethlehem, to the house of Jesse. \"I have chosen one of his sons to be king.\""},{"sc":"tents","n":"Jesse's oldest son, Eliab, walked in. Tall, strong, handsome. Samuel thought, \"Surely this is the one!\""},{"sc":"tents","n":"But God said: \"Don't look at his appearance or his height. People look at the outside, but the Lord looks at the heart.\""},{"sc":"tents","n":"Seven sons passed in front of Samuel. God said no to each one. \"Are these all your sons?\" \"Well, there's the youngest. He's out looking after the sheep.\""},{"sc":"field","n":"They fetched David, ruddy-cheeked with bright eyes. God said: \"This is the one. Anoint him!\" Samuel poured oil on his head in front of his brothers, and the Spirit of the Lord came powerfully on David."}],"lesson":{"title":"God looks at the heart","text":"Nobody even invited David to the meeting. But God had been watching him, alone with the sheep, faithful in small things. God doesn't choose leaders by looks, age or popularity. He looks at the heart."},"order":["God sends Samuel to Bethlehem","Eliab walks in","God says, \"Look at the heart\"","Seven sons are rejected","David is fetched from the sheep","Samuel anoints David"],"quiz":[{"q":"Which town did Samuel go to?","o":["Bethlehem","Jericho","Shiloh","Gath"],"why":"1 Samuel 16:4."},{"q":"Where was David when Samuel came?","o":["Looking after the sheep","At the palace","In the army","Asleep"],"why":"1 Samuel 16:11."},{"q":"What does the Lord look at?","o":["The heart","Height","Looks","Clothes"],"why":"1 Samuel 16:7."}],"words":["DAVID","JESSE","HEART","ANOINT","SHEEP","YOUNGEST"]},"s1n":{"passage":[[16,14,23]],"intro":[{"sc":"throne","n":"Now the Spirit of the Lord had left Saul, and an evil spirit troubled him. He became gloomy, angry and afraid."},{"sc":"throne","w":"bpeople","e":"worried","t":"My lord, let us find someone who plays the harp well. When the dark mood comes, the music will make you feel better."},{"sc":"throne","n":"One servant knew just the person: \"Jesse's son David. He plays well, he's brave, he speaks well, he's handsome, and the Lord is with him.\""},{"sc":"throne","n":"So the shepherd boy came to the palace. Whenever Saul's dark moods came, David played his harp, and Saul felt refreshed, and the evil spirit left him. Saul loved David, and made him his armour-bearer."}],"lesson":{"title":"Bring peace into dark places","text":"Nobody knew David had just been anointed the next king. He simply served Saul with his gift. Music and kindness brought peace to a troubled man. Leaders use their gifts to serve, even those who are struggling."},"order":["The Spirit of the Lord leaves Saul","Saul becomes troubled and gloomy","His servants suggest a harp player","They choose David","David plays and Saul feels better"],"quiz":[{"q":"What instrument did David play?","o":["The harp","The drum","The trumpet","The flute"],"why":"1 Samuel 16:23."},{"q":"What happened when David played?","o":["Saul felt refreshed and the evil spirit left","Saul fell asleep","Saul got angry","Nothing"],"why":"1 Samuel 16:23."},{"q":"What job did Saul give David?","o":["Armour-bearer","Cook","General","Priest"],"why":"1 Samuel 16:21."}],"words":["HARP","MUSIC","PEACE","SAUL","PALACE","SERVE"]},"s1o":{"passage":[[17,4,11],[17,32,51]],"intro":[{"sc":"elah","n":"Two armies faced each other across the Valley of Elah. Every morning and evening for forty days, a Philistine giant named Goliath stepped out and shouted."},{"sc":"elah","w":"bgoliath","e":"frown","t":"Choose a man and let him come and fight me! If he wins, we'll be your slaves. If I win, you'll be ours!"},{"sc":"elah","n":"He was nearly three metres tall, with a bronze helmet, armour as heavy as a man, and a spear like a weaver's beam. Every soldier was terrified."},{"sc":"elah","n":"Young David arrived bringing food for his brothers. He heard the giant's insults. \"Who is this man, to defy the armies of the living God?\""},{"sc":"elah","w":"bdavid","e":"stern","t":"The Lord who rescued me from the lion and the bear will rescue me from this Philistine!"},{"sc":"elah","n":"David tried on Saul's armour, but it was too big. He took his shepherd's staff, his sling, and five smooth stones from the stream."},{"sc":"elah","w":"bdavid","e":"stern","t":"You come to me with sword and spear, but I come to you in the name of the Lord! The battle is the Lord's!"},{"sc":"elah","n":"David ran towards the giant, put a stone in his sling, and let it fly. It struck Goliath in the forehead, and the giant fell face down on the ground!"}],"lesson":{"title":"Big faith beats big problems","text":"Everyone saw how big Goliath was. David saw how big God was. He used the skills he'd learned faithfully in small, hidden places, fighting lions and bears. Leaders face giants with faith, and with the tools God has trained them to use."},"order":["Goliath challenges Israel for forty days","David brings food for his brothers","David offers to fight","David refuses Saul's armour","He picks five smooth stones","David's stone strikes Goliath"],"quiz":[{"q":"How many stones did David pick up?","o":["Five","One","Three","Twelve"],"why":"1 Samuel 17:40."},{"q":"Why didn't David wear Saul's armour?","o":["He wasn't used to it, and it didn't fit","It was broken","Saul said no","He forgot"],"why":"1 Samuel 17:39."},{"q":"What had David fought before?","o":["A lion and a bear","Giants","Soldiers","Dragons"],"why":"1 Samuel 17:34-36."}],"words":["GOLIATH","SLING","STONES","GIANT","ELAH","COURAGE"]},"s1p":{"passage":[[18,1,4],[20,1,4],[20,30,42]],"intro":[{"sc":"throne","n":"After Goliath, Saul's son Jonathan and David became best friends. Jonathan loved David as much as himself. He gave David his own robe, armour, sword, bow and belt."},{"sc":"throne","n":"That was amazing, because Jonathan was the prince, the next in line to be king. And he could see that God had chosen David instead."},{"sc":"arrows","n":"When Saul turned against David, the two friends made a secret plan: \"I'll shoot three arrows. If I tell my boy, 'The arrows are on this side', you're safe. If I say 'The arrows are beyond you', run!\""},{"sc":"arrows","n":"Jonathan found out Saul really wanted to kill David. He went to the field and shot the arrows. \"The arrow is beyond you! Hurry! Don't stop!\""},{"sc":"arrows","w":"bjonathan","e":"worried","t":"Go in peace. The Lord is witness between you and me, and between our children, for ever."}],"lesson":{"title":"Friendship without jealousy","text":"Jonathan had every reason to be jealous of David: David would get the crown that was supposed to be his. Instead, he protected him, encouraged him and gave him his best. True friends cheer for each other, even when it costs them."},"order":["Jonathan and David become best friends","Jonathan gives David his robe and weapons","Saul turns against David","They make a secret arrow signal","Jonathan shoots the arrows","The friends say a sad goodbye"],"quiz":[{"q":"What did Jonathan give David?","o":["His robe, armour, sword, bow and belt","A horse","Gold","A crown"],"why":"1 Samuel 18:4."},{"q":"What was their secret signal?","o":["Arrows shot in a field","A song","A letter","A fire"],"why":"1 Samuel 20:20-22."},{"q":"Why was Jonathan's friendship so special?","o":["David would become king instead of him, and he wasn't jealous","He was rich","He was older","He was a giant"],"why":"Real friendship."}],"words":["FRIEND","JONATHAN","ARROWS","LOYAL","BOW","PEACE"]},"s1q":{"passage":[[18,6,12],[19,9,17]],"intro":[{"sc":"citygate","n":"When David came home from battles, the women danced and sang: \"Saul has killed his thousands, and David his tens of thousands!\""},{"sc":"citygate","w":"bsaul","e":"frown","t":"They give David ten thousands, and me only thousands? What more can he get but the kingdom?"},{"sc":"throne","n":"Saul wanted David dead, so he set a dangerous bride price for Michal: proof that David had defeated a hundred Philistines. Saul hoped the Philistines would kill him! But David and his men brought proof of two hundred, double the price. Saul's plan failed, and he feared David even more."},{"sc":"throne","n":"From that day, Saul kept a jealous eye on David. One day, while David played his harp, Saul threw a spear at him! David dodged it, twice."},{"sc":"throne","n":"David married Saul's daughter, Michal. One night, Saul sent soldiers to watch David's house and kill him in the morning."},{"sc":"throne","w":"bmichal","e":"worried","t":"If you don't escape tonight, you'll be dead tomorrow!"},{"sc":"throne","n":"Michal let David down through a window, and he escaped. Then she put a statue in his bed, with goat's hair on its head and a blanket on top. \"He's sick!\" she told the soldiers. By the time they found out, David was long gone."}],"lesson":{"title":"Jealousy turns friends into enemies","text":"Saul couldn't stand someone else being praised. His jealousy grew until he tried to kill the very person who served him best. Leaders celebrate other people's success instead of feeling threatened by it."},"order":["The women sing about David's tens of thousands","Saul becomes jealous","Saul throws a spear at David","David marries Michal","Michal helps David escape through a window","She puts a statue in his bed"],"quiz":[{"q":"What did the women sing?","o":["\"Saul has killed thousands, David tens of thousands\"","\"Long live Saul\"","\"Goliath is coming\"","\"Hallelujah\""],"why":"1 Samuel 18:7."},{"q":"What did Saul throw at David?","o":["A spear","A stone","A cup","A shoe"],"why":"1 Samuel 18:11."},{"q":"What did Michal put in David's bed?","o":["A statue with goat's hair","Pillows","A sheep","Her brother"],"why":"1 Samuel 19:13."}],"words":["JEALOUS","SPEAR","MICHAL","WINDOW","ESCAPE","STATUE"]},"s1q2":{"passage":[[10,9,13],[19,1,7],[19,18,24]],"intro":[{"sc":"tents","n":"Back when Saul was first anointed, he met a group of prophets playing music and praising God, and he joined in! People were amazed: \"Is Saul among the prophets?\" It became a famous saying."},{"sc":"throne","w":"bsaul","e":"frown","t":"I want David dead. Every one of you, find him and kill him!"},{"sc":"throne","w":"bjonathan","e":"stern","t":"Father, don't sin against David! He's never wronged you. He risked his life to kill Goliath, and you were glad! Why kill an innocent man?"},{"sc":"throne","n":"Saul listened, and swore, \"As the Lord lives, David will not be put to death.\" For a while, there was peace."},{"sc":"tents","n":"But Saul's jealousy came back. David fled to Samuel at Naioth. Saul sent soldiers to capture him, but when they arrived, God's Spirit came on them, and they started prophesying! Three groups of soldiers, the same thing each time!"},{"sc":"tents","n":"Finally Saul went himself, and the Spirit came on him too. He lay on the ground all day and night, prophesying. Once again people said, \"Is Saul also among the prophets?\""}],"lesson":{"title":"Speak up for the innocent","text":"Jonathan risked his father's anger to defend his friend, and for a while it worked. And God protected David in an amazing way: the soldiers sent to catch him ended up worshipping instead! Leaders speak up for the innocent, and trust God to protect."},"order":["Saul prophesies with the prophets","Saul orders David's death","Jonathan defends David","Saul promises not to kill David","Soldiers sent after David start prophesying","Saul prophesies too"],"quiz":[{"q":"What became a famous saying about Saul?","o":["\"Is Saul among the prophets?\"","\"Saul is the tallest\"","\"Saul has a spear\"","\"Where is Saul?\""],"why":"1 Samuel 10:12."},{"q":"Who defended David to Saul?","o":["Jonathan","Michal","Abner","Doeg"],"why":"1 Samuel 19:4."},{"q":"What happened to the soldiers sent to catch David at Naioth?","o":["They started prophesying","They caught him","They ran away","They fell asleep"],"why":"1 Samuel 19:20."}],"words":["PROPHETS","NAIOTH","JONATHAN","DEFEND","SPIRIT","INNOCENT"]},"s1r":{"passage":[[21,1,15]],"intro":[{"sc":"tabernacle","n":"David ran for his life, with nothing. He came to the priest Ahimelech at Nob, hungry."},{"sc":"tabernacle","n":"The only bread there was the holy bread from God's table. The priest gave it to David and his men. He also gave him a famous weapon: the very sword of Goliath!"},{"sc":"tabernacle","n":"But one of Saul's servants, Doeg the Edomite, was there that day, watching."},{"sc":"citygate","n":"David fled to the Philistine city of Gath, Goliath's home town! When the guards recognised him, he was terrified."},{"sc":"citygate","n":"So David pretended to be mad. He scribbled on the gate doors and let spit run down his beard! The king said, \"Do I need more madmen? Get him out of here!\" David escaped, and later wrote Psalm 34 about that day."}],"lesson":{"title":"God protects you when you're afraid","text":"David the giant-slayer was now afraid and on the run. Even in his scariest moments, God provided bread, a sword and an escape. Later David wrote, \"I sought the Lord, and He answered me.\" Brave people feel fear too; they take it to God."},"order":["David runs from Saul","The priest gives him holy bread","David gets Goliath's sword","Doeg is watching","David flees to Gath","David pretends to be mad"],"quiz":[{"q":"Whose sword was David given?","o":["Goliath's","Saul's","Jonathan's","Samuel's"],"why":"1 Samuel 21:9."},{"q":"Where did David flee?","o":["Gath, Goliath's home town","Egypt","Jerusalem","Bethlehem"],"why":"1 Samuel 21:10."},{"q":"How did David escape from Gath?","o":["He pretended to be mad","He fought his way out","He hid in a basket","He flew"],"why":"1 Samuel 21:13."}],"words":["BREAD","SWORD","GATH","DOEG","ESCAPE","PSALM"]},"s1s":{"passage":[[22,1,5],[22,9,23]],"intro":[{"sc":"cave","n":"David hid in the cave of Adullam. His family came to join him, and then something surprising happened: about 400 men came too."},{"sc":"cave","n":"They were people in trouble, people in debt, and people who were unhappy. David became their leader. Many of them would later become his famous 'mighty men'."},{"sc":"throne","n":"Meanwhile, Doeg the Edomite told Saul that the priest had helped David. Saul was furious. He ordered his guards to kill the priests. They refused! But Doeg did it, killing 85 priests and attacking their whole town of Nob."},{"sc":"cave","n":"Only one priest's son, Abiathar, escaped and ran to David."},{"sc":"cave","w":"bdavid","e":"worried","t":"I knew Doeg was there that day. This is my fault. Stay with me. Don't be afraid. You'll be safe with me."}],"lesson":{"title":"Lead the 'misfits' well","text":"David's army started as a crowd of troubled, in-debt and unhappy people. He shaped them into heroes. And when terrible things happened, he took responsibility and protected the survivor. Leaders see potential in people others give up on."},"order":["David hides in the cave of Adullam","His family joins him","400 troubled men come to him","Doeg tells Saul about the priest","Doeg kills the priests of Nob","Abiathar escapes to David"],"quiz":[{"q":"Who came to David at the cave?","o":["People in trouble, in debt and unhappy","Kings","Priests only","Philistines"],"why":"1 Samuel 22:2."},{"q":"Who refused Saul's order to kill the priests?","o":["Saul's own guards","Doeg","Jonathan","Nobody"],"why":"1 Samuel 22:17."},{"q":"Who escaped and ran to David?","o":["Abiathar","Doeg","Ahimelech","Goliath"],"why":"1 Samuel 22:20."}],"words":["CAVE","ADULLAM","DOEG","ABIATHAR","MIGHTY","PROTECT"]},"s1t2":{"passage":[[23,1,5],[23,14,18],[23,24,28]],"intro":[{"sc":"ploughfield","n":"The Philistines were robbing the threshing floors of a town called Keilah. David asked God, \"Shall I go and save them?\" God said yes. David's men were scared, so he asked again. God said, \"Go. I will give the Philistines into your hand.\" They rescued the town."},{"sc":"wilderness","n":"Then David hid in the desert of Ziph. Saul searched for him every day."},{"sc":"wilderness","w":"bjonathan","e":"smile","t":"Don't be afraid. My father won't find you. You will be king over Israel, and I'll be next to you. Even my father knows it."},{"sc":"wilderness","n":"Jonathan helped David find strength in God. The two friends made a promise before the Lord. It was the last time they would ever meet."},{"sc":"cliffs","n":"The people of Ziph betrayed David's hiding place. Saul's army chased him around a mountain: David on one side, Saul on the other, getting closer and closer..."},{"sc":"cliffs","n":"Just as Saul was about to catch him, a messenger ran up: \"Hurry! The Philistines are attacking the land!\" Saul had to turn back. They called the place 'the Rock of Escape'."}],"lesson":{"title":"Strengthen your friends in God","text":"David was exhausted and hunted. Jonathan didn't just cheer him up; he helped him find strength in God. True friends point each other to God when things are hard."},"order":["The Philistines attack Keilah","David asks God twice","David saves Keilah","Jonathan strengthens David in God","Saul chases David around a mountain","A messenger makes Saul turn back"],"quiz":[{"q":"How many times did David ask God about Keilah?","o":["Twice","Once","Seven times","Never"],"why":"1 Samuel 23:2-4."},{"q":"What did Jonathan help David do?","o":["Find strength in God","Escape to Egypt","Fight Saul","Become king at once"],"why":"1 Samuel 23:16."},{"q":"What saved David at the mountain?","o":["A messenger said the Philistines were attacking","A storm","An angel","Jonathan"],"why":"1 Samuel 23:27."}],"words":["KEILAH","ZIPH","MOUNTAIN","ESCAPE","STRENGTH","FRIEND"]},"s1t":{"passage":[[24,1,22]],"intro":[{"sc":"wilderness","n":"Saul took 3,000 of his best soldiers to hunt David down in the desert near En-gedi."},{"sc":"cave","n":"Saul went into a cave to go to the toilet, not knowing that David and his men were hiding deep inside that very cave!"},{"sc":"cave","w":"bpeople","e":"big","t":"This is your chance! God has handed your enemy to you!"},{"sc":"cave","n":"David crept up silently, and cut off a corner of Saul's robe. Then he felt terrible, even for that. \"I will not raise my hand against the Lord's anointed king.\""},{"sc":"cave","w":"bdavid","e":"stern","t":"My lord the king! Look, a piece of your robe! I could have killed you, but I didn't. Let the Lord judge between us."},{"sc":"cave","w":"bsaul","e":"worried","t":"Is that your voice, David, my son? You are more righteous than I am."}],"lesson":{"title":"Don't grab what God will give","text":"David had the perfect chance for revenge, and his men urged him to take it. But he refused to hurt Saul, trusting God to make him king in God's way and time. Leaders don't take shortcuts that involve doing wrong."},"order":["Saul hunts David with 3,000 soldiers","Saul goes into a cave","David's men urge him to strike","David cuts off a corner of Saul's robe","David calls out to Saul","Saul admits David is more righteous"],"quiz":[{"q":"Why did Saul go into the cave?","o":["To go to the toilet","To hide","To sleep","To pray"],"why":"1 Samuel 24:3."},{"q":"What did David cut off?","o":["A corner of Saul's robe","Saul's hair","Saul's crown","A rope"],"why":"1 Samuel 24:4."},{"q":"What did Saul say to David?","o":["\"You are more righteous than I am\"","\"I'll kill you\"","\"Go away\"","Nothing"],"why":"1 Samuel 24:17."}],"words":["CAVE","ROBE","SPARE","ENGEDI","MERCY","ANOINTED"]},"s1u":{"passage":[[25,2,13],[25,18,35],[25,36,39]],"intro":[{"sc":"wilderness","n":"A very rich man named Nabal had 3,000 sheep. His name meant 'fool', and he lived up to it. But his wife, Abigail, was wise and beautiful."},{"sc":"wilderness","n":"David's men had protected Nabal's shepherds in the desert. At sheep-shearing time, a time of feasting, David politely asked for some food."},{"sc":"wilderness","w":"bnabal","e":"smirk","t":"Who is this David? There are lots of runaway servants these days! Why should I give my food to strangers?"},{"sc":"wilderness","n":"David was furious. He strapped on his sword and set off with 400 men to destroy Nabal's whole household."},{"sc":"wilderness","n":"A servant ran to Abigail. Quickly, she loaded donkeys with 200 loaves, wine, five roasted sheep, grain, raisin cakes and fig cakes, and rode out to meet David."},{"sc":"wilderness","w":"babigail","e":"worried","t":"My lord, please ignore that foolish man. Don't let this be on your conscience when you become king: that you took revenge yourself."},{"sc":"wilderness","w":"bdavidw","e":"smile","t":"Blessed be the Lord who sent you! And blessed be your good sense, which kept me from bloodshed today."},{"sc":"wilderness","n":"When Nabal sobered up and heard what had happened, his heart failed, and ten days later he died. David then asked Abigail to be his wife."}],"lesson":{"title":"Wisdom calms the storm","text":"Nabal's rudeness nearly caused a massacre. David's anger nearly made him do something terrible. Abigail's quick thinking, generosity and wise words saved everyone. Leaders listen to wise counsel, even when they're angry, and they step in to make peace."},"order":["David's men protect Nabal's shepherds","David asks Nabal for food","Nabal insults David","David sets off with 400 men","Abigail rides out with gifts","David thanks God for Abigail's good sense"],"quiz":[{"q":"What does the name Nabal mean?","o":["Fool","Rich","Shepherd","Strong"],"why":"1 Samuel 25:25."},{"q":"What did Abigail bring David?","o":["Bread, wine, sheep, grain and cakes","Gold","Swords","Nothing"],"why":"1 Samuel 25:18."},{"q":"What did David thank Abigail for?","o":["Her good sense, which stopped him from bloodshed","Her beauty","Her gold","Her donkeys"],"why":"1 Samuel 25:33."}],"words":["ABIGAIL","NABAL","FOOL","WISDOM","PEACE","GIFTS"]},"s1v":{"passage":[[26,5,25]],"intro":[{"sc":"nightcamp","n":"Saul was hunting David again, with 3,000 soldiers. That night, the whole army fell into a deep sleep from the Lord."},{"sc":"nightcamp","n":"David and his brave friend Abishai crept right into the middle of the camp. There lay King Saul, asleep, with his spear stuck in the ground by his head and a water jug beside him."},{"sc":"nightcamp","w":"bpeople","e":"stern","t":"Let me pin him to the ground with his own spear. Just one strike!"},{"sc":"nightcamp","w":"bdavid","e":"stern","t":"No! Don't harm him. Just take the spear and the water jug, and let's go."},{"sc":"battlehill","n":"From a hilltop far away, David shouted: \"Abner! Some guard you are! Where's the king's spear? Where's his water jug?\""}],"lesson":{"title":"Integrity when no one would know","text":"For the second time, David could have ended his troubles. Nobody would have stopped him. But he refused to do wrong to get what God had promised. Leaders keep their integrity even when they could get away with doing wrong."},"order":["Saul hunts David again","The army falls into a deep sleep","David and Abishai sneak into the camp","Abishai wants to strike Saul","David takes the spear and water jug","David calls out from the hilltop"],"quiz":[{"q":"What did David take from the sleeping Saul?","o":["His spear and water jug","His crown","His sword","His robe"],"why":"1 Samuel 26:12."},{"q":"Who went with David into the camp?","o":["Abishai","Jonathan","Joab","Samuel"],"why":"1 Samuel 26:6."},{"q":"Why did the whole army stay asleep?","o":["A deep sleep from the Lord fell on them","They were drunk","They were sick","It was very late"],"why":"1 Samuel 26:12."}],"words":["SPEAR","JUG","ABISHAI","SLEEP","CAMP","INTEGRITY"]},"s1v2":{"passage":[[27,1,7],[29,1,11]],"intro":[{"sc":"wilderness","n":"David grew tired of running. He thought, \"One day Saul will catch me. The best thing is to escape to the land of the Philistines.\""},{"sc":"throne","n":"So David took his 600 men and their families to King Achish of Gath. Achish gave him the little town of Ziklag. They lived there for a year and four months."},{"sc":"battlehill","n":"Then the Philistines prepared a big war against Israel. Achish trusted David so much that he brought him along as his bodyguard!"},{"sc":"battlehill","n":"But the other Philistine commanders were furious: \"What are these Hebrews doing here? Isn't this the David they sang about: 'Saul killed thousands, and David tens of thousands'? He'll turn against us in the battle!\""},{"sc":"throne","w":"bachish","e":"worried","t":"You've been as good as an angel of God to me, David. But the commanders won't let you fight. Go home in the morning."}],"lesson":{"title":"God protects you from impossible situations","text":"David got himself into a tricky spot, marching with Israel's enemies against his own people. God used the suspicious Philistine commanders to send him home, so he never had to fight Israel. Even when we make unwise choices, God can make a way out."},"order":["David gets tired of running","He escapes to King Achish","Achish gives him Ziklag","The Philistines prepare for war","The commanders refuse to let David fight","Achish sends David home"],"quiz":[{"q":"Which town did Achish give David?","o":["Ziklag","Gath","Hebron","Bethlehem"],"why":"1 Samuel 27:6."},{"q":"Why didn't the Philistine commanders trust David?","o":["They remembered the song about his tens of thousands","He was too young","He was sick","He was rich"],"why":"1 Samuel 29:5."},{"q":"What did Achish compare David to?","o":["An angel of God","A lion","A giant","A fox"],"why":"1 Samuel 29:9."}],"words":["ACHISH","GATH","ZIKLAG","PHILISTINES","COMMANDERS","HOME"]},"s1w":{"passage":[[28,3,25]],"intro":[{"sc":"endor","n":"Samuel had died, and all Israel mourned him. Now a huge Philistine army had come, and Saul was terrified. He prayed, but God didn't answer: no dreams, no prophets."},{"sc":"endor","n":"Saul had banned all mediums, people who claim to talk to the dead, because God forbids it. But now, desperate, he disguised himself and went at night to a medium in the town of Endor."},{"sc":"endor","w":"bsaul","e":"worried","t":"Bring up Samuel for me."},{"sc":"endor","w":"bmedium","e":"shock","t":"I see a spirit coming up out of the earth! An old man wrapped in a robe! ...You're Saul! Why have you tricked me?"},{"sc":"endor","n":"The message Saul heard was terrible: \"The Lord has torn the kingdom from you and given it to David. Tomorrow you and your sons will be with me.\""},{"sc":"endor","n":"Saul fell flat on the ground, weak with fear and hunger. The woman made him a meal, and he went out into the night."}],"lesson":{"title":"Don't look for answers in the dark","text":"When God was silent, Saul turned to something God had forbidden, the very thing he had banned himself. Desperation made him break his own rules. Leaders stay faithful even when God seems silent, and they never seek guidance from forbidden places."},"order":["Samuel dies","A huge Philistine army comes","God doesn't answer Saul","Saul disguises himself","He visits the woman of Endor","Saul hears a terrible message"],"quiz":[{"q":"Why did Saul go to the medium?","o":["God wasn't answering him and he was desperate","He was curious","Samuel told him to","For fun"],"why":"1 Samuel 28:6."},{"q":"What had Saul done to mediums before?","o":["Banned them from the land","Hired them","Invited them","Nothing"],"why":"1 Samuel 28:3."},{"q":"How did Saul go to Endor?","o":["Disguised, at night","With his army","In his chariot","With Samuel"],"why":"1 Samuel 28:8."}],"words":["ENDOR","MEDIUM","NIGHT","DISGUISE","SILENT","SAUL"]},"s1x":{"passage":[[30,1,8],[30,16,25]],"intro":[{"sc":"ruinsfire","n":"David and his men came home to their town of Ziklag and found it burned to the ground. Raiders had taken all their wives and children!"},{"sc":"ruinsfire","n":"The men wept until they had no strength left to cry. Then, in their grief, they turned on David and talked about stoning him."},{"sc":"ruinsfire","n":"But David found strength in the Lord his God. He asked God, \"Should I chase them?\" God said, \"Go. You will rescue them all.\""},{"sc":"wilderness","n":"On the way, they found an Egyptian lying in a field, sick and starving. They gave him water, bread, figs and raisins. He was the raiders' slave, abandoned when he got sick! He showed them exactly where the raiders were camped."},{"sc":"wilderness","n":"They found the raiders feasting, and rescued every single person, and everything that had been taken. Nothing was missing!"},{"sc":"wilderness","w":"bdavidw","e":"stern","t":"The men who stayed behind guarding the supplies get exactly the same share as those who went into battle. Everyone shares alike!"}],"lesson":{"title":"Strengthen yourself in God","text":"Everything was gone, and his own men turned against him. David didn't give up or lash out. He found strength in God first, then led. And he made sure the tired men who stayed behind were treated fairly. Leaders find strength in God, and they're fair to everyone on the team."},"order":["David's men find Ziklag burned","Their families have been taken","The men turn against David","David finds strength in God","They rescue everyone","David shares the spoil fairly"],"quiz":[{"q":"What had happened to Ziklag?","o":["Raiders had burned it and taken the families","A flood","An earthquake","Nothing"],"why":"1 Samuel 30:1-3."},{"q":"What did David do when his men turned against him?","o":["Found strength in the Lord his God","Ran away","Fought them","Gave up"],"why":"1 Samuel 30:6."},{"q":"Who got a share of the spoil?","o":["Everyone, including those who guarded supplies","Only the fighters","Only David","Nobody"],"why":"1 Samuel 30:24."}],"words":["ZIKLAG","STRENGTH","RESCUE","FAIR","SHARE","RAIDERS"]},"s1y":{"passage":[[31,1,13]],"intro":[{"sc":"gilboa","n":"The Philistines attacked Israel on Mount Gilboa. Israel's army ran, and many fell. Saul's sons, including brave Jonathan, were killed in the fighting."},{"sc":"gilboa","n":"Saul was badly wounded by archers. Rather than be captured and mocked by his enemies, he fell on his own sword, and his armour-bearer did the same."},{"sc":"gilboa","n":"The next day the Philistines found Saul's body and hung it on the wall of their city, Beth-shan, to boast."},{"sc":"gilboa","n":"But the people of Jabesh-gilead remembered how Saul had rescued them at the very start of his reign. Their bravest men marched all night, took down the bodies of Saul and his sons, and gave them a proper burial."}],"lesson":{"title":"How you finish matters","text":"Saul began humble and brave, but disobedience, jealousy and turning from God led to a tragic end. Yet the town he rescued at the start never forgot his kindness. Leaders want to finish well, and the good we do is remembered."},"order":["The Philistines attack on Mount Gilboa","Jonathan is killed in battle","Saul is badly wounded","Saul falls on his own sword","The Philistines hang his body on a wall","The men of Jabesh bury Saul and his sons"],"quiz":[{"q":"Where was Saul's last battle?","o":["Mount Gilboa","Mount Sinai","The Jordan","Jericho"],"why":"1 Samuel 31:1."},{"q":"Who remembered Saul's kindness and buried him?","o":["The people of Jabesh-gilead","The Philistines","David's men","Samuel"],"why":"1 Samuel 31:11-13."},{"q":"Why did the people of Jabesh do this?","o":["Saul had rescued them at the start of his reign","They were paid","David told them to","They were afraid"],"why":"Remember 1 Samuel 11?"}],"words":["GILBOA","SAUL","JONATHAN","JABESH","BURIAL","FINISH"]}});
